I am standing in the station in front of the machine.
I must buy a ticket.
My journey with the U-Bahn and the S-Bahn costs three Euro fifty.
I only need one ticket for the whole journey.
I have to change trains later.
But this ticket is valid for everything.
I press on the screen.
Nothing happens.
Then I see a small sign.
The machine is out of order.
A woman is standing next to me.
She sees my problem.
"The machine does not work," she says.
"At the end of the platform there is another machine."
She points over there.
"Oh, thank you very much," I say.
I walk quickly to the other machine.
I must hurry.
Here the screen works.
I buy my ticket.
